2026-10-31T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2377) 'Each platform links its own baked translation into the addon, so the web game loads.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2377) 'Chrome refuses to compile a WebAssembly module larger than 8 MB on the main thread, and a game's translation is larger. C baked on one platform does not match on another.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2377) 'Bake the C of a platform by running the game once on that platform with the emitter on, then compile the emitted C for that platform.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2377) 'a translation links into the addon, one bake per platform
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2377) '- A translation can be compiled into the addon library of its platform instead of being loaded as a library at run time. On the web this is the only route that works. The desktop builds of the same game use the same route.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2377) '- Each platform bakes its own C. The game runs once on that platform with the emitter on, and the emitted C is compiled for that platform.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2377) '- RFD66606-2294, where this rule lived before the split.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2377) 'Where the objects live
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2377) 'The addon keeps each platform's translation objects in a folder of their own, `src/bintr/<platform>.<arch>/`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2377) 'Why each platform bakes
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2377) 'The program hash covers the machine layout as well as the program, so C baked on one platform does not match on another. Windows and Linux on x86_64 share a layout and a hash, and each still compiles its own copy. One bake of the SolidCraft guest is 32 C files, 336 MB of C for 16.2 MB of RISC-V code.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2377) 'A change to the host's system calls
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2377) 'A change to the host's system calls leaves the guest's translation as it was, so the compiled objects and the hash stay valid and only a relink is needed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2377) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2377) 'Chrome refuses to compile a WebAssembly module larger than 8 MB on the main thread, and a game's translation is larger.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

